portfolio_flickr stopped working on PHP 7.4 and upward due to the fatal error because we're trying to serialize CURLFile class, which does not allow anymore.
{code:java}
Unserialization of CURLFile instances is not allowed. As of PHP 7.4.0, serialization is forbidden in the first place.
{code}
Refer: [https://www.php.net/manual/en/class.curlfile.php]

Sometimes we want to highlight a tab in one of the navigation views when it does not match the set url for that navigation node.

Currently making this work requires a lot of additional code and overwriting the views.

To try and help third party developers (and ourselves) let's provide a simple method that can be called to set the active tab.

Something like:
{code}
$PAGE->set_secondary_active_tab($navkey);
{code}
Where the navkey is the key given to the node that represents the tab we want active.
This could be useful for the primary navigation as well.

Since recently (MDL-72594 landed), we are getting random failures (often) with this scenario:

{{Next 30 days in course view}}

Link: https://ci.moodle.org/job/W.03.02%20-%20Behat%20-%20Chrome%20+%20MySQLi/1045/

{code}
001 Scenario: Next 30 days in course view                    # /var/www/html/blocks/timeline/tests/behat/block_timeline_courses.feature:39
      Then I should see "Course 1" in the "Timeline" "block" # /var/www/html/blocks/timeline/tests/behat/block_timeline_courses.feature:45
        "Course 1" text was found in the "Timeline" element but was not visible (Behat\Mink\Exception\ExpectationException)
{code}

It seems to be chrome-only, though that's not assured. For reference, a failure in the same scenario was reported when the timeline block was originally unveiled / split. See MDL-63044. I may/may not be related.

It seems that a navigation node of type "{{TYPE_CONTAINER}}" can no longer have any children, and the action of the first (I believe) child is used instead.

You can see an example of this in the Forum with the "Subscription mode" container.

Replication
# Create a new forum
# View the forum
## *Observe: "{{Subscription mode}}" is a link which does not expand to give options*
# Click the "Subscription mode" navigation link
## *Observe: the mode is toggled between Optional and Automatic"
## *Observe: there is no way to set the mode to "Forced" or "Disabled" from the More menu*


Alternatively, add some code like this to the bottom of {{mod/forum/lib.php::forum_extend_settings_navigation()}}
{code}
    $nodes = [];
    $nodes[] = \navigation_node::create('Example.com', 'https://example.com', \navigation_node::TYPE_SETTING, null, 'COM');
    $nodes[] = \navigation_node::create('Example.org', 'https://example.org', \navigation_node::TYPE_SETTING, null, 'ORG');

    $addto = $forumnode->add(
        'Some new parent container',
        null,
        \navigation_node::TYPE_CONTAINER
    );

    foreach ($nodes as $node) {
        $addto->add_node($node);
    }
{code}
Observe how the "SOme new parent container" is not a container but is now a link for the first child item.

