As raised by Iñigo and Helen in the moodle.org forums ([https://lang.moodle.org/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=9554]), the new strings added to langconfig.php as part of MDL-83873:
{quote}$string['strftimerelativetoday'] = 'Today, %d %B';
$string['strftimerelativetomorrow'] = 'Tomorrow, %d %B';
$string['strftimerelativeyesterday'] = 'Yesterday, %d %B'
{quote}
the words Today, Tomorrow and Yesterday can't be translated by translators and will always display in English and not the language of the user.

!upcoming events with untranslated text.png|thumbnail!

This problem is reported as MDL-79461 and may be resolved by MDL-79545.

However, for now, these strings should be moved to a different place to guarantee they can be translated properly.

To meet the WCAG Level AA Success Criterion 4.1.3—Status Messages, we must ensure that we inform users of the processing result whenever an AI action has generated results.

From the auditors:
{quote}
When the site returns results generated by AI, the result is displayed on the screen, but assistive technology does not inform the user that the process has been completed.
{quote}

This applies to both Generate text and Generate image AI actions. This may also apply to the Explain (5.0 only) and Summarise actions.

