In MDL-84450 the compatibility helper for Boostrap v4 > v5 data-attributes was created, but exporting the function {{initBootstrap4Compatibility}} as {{default}} in [bs4-compat.js:184|https://github.com/roland04/moodle/commit/1d452ce4cab1eb3a66d95f9016f61e82941f22de#diff-ad3f7145c8b0679492ec51e91ecf3fd6e1e60f78045feea89193ce5db947e055R184] was incorrect, because then initialising it through {{$PAGE->requires->js_call_amd('theme_boost/bs4-compat', 'initBootstrap4Compatibility');}} is not possible.

Thanks [~accountid:712020:c3923c80-3d9c-4f06-b36d-e40eb1e91308] for raising it in [Matrix Moodle Dev chat|https://matrix.to/#/!rKYzebaIslXxIYwCfo:moodle.com/$vieLM_Q5HubElMy0nSFQGtpvL8--0PMieMMQAlwIUlI?via=moodle.com&via=matrix.org&via=matrix.eledia.de]

Remove "default" and rename the method as "init", so it can be initialised like:
*.mustache*
{code:mustache}{{#js}}
require(['theme_boost/bs4-compat'], function(BS4Compat) {
    BS4Compat.init();
});
{{/js}}
{code}
*.js*
{code:js}import * as BS4Compat from './bs4-compat';
BS4Compat.init();
{code}
*.php*
{code:js}$PAGE->requires->js_call_amd('theme_boost/bs4-compat', 'init');
{code}

In display options, an UL list is opened right after the form tag : 

        $html = html_writer::start_tag('form', $attributes);
        *$html .= html_writer::start_tag('ul', array('class' => 'choices list-unstyled unstyled'));*

closed just before adding a clearfloat div : 

        $html .= html_writer::tag('li','', array('class'=>'clearfloat'));
        *$html .= html_writer::end_tag('ul');*

But additionally closed again at end before closing the form : 

        *$html .= html_writer::end_tag('ul');*
        $html .= html_writer::end_tag('form');

Removing last closing occurrence make things fine.

To have it properly detected for the future, it would be great to add to all the upgrade.php scripts some lines like these:

{code:php}
// Automatically generated Moodle v5.0.0 release upgrade line.
// Put any upgrade step following this.
{code}

exactly before the "{{return true;}}" present in all the scripts.

Normally, it's ok to do that both in the stable (500_STABLE) and the {{main}} branches, so they will allow quickly find where 5.0.0 started and act once we decide future requirements.

But, *when under parallel development, this only can be done in the stable (500_STABLE) branch* as the {{main}} branch already has diverged and can have own upgrade steps not corresponding to the version just released, but to the future version being developed in parallel.

The change can be performed globally with:

{code:bash}
#!/bin/bash
export rel="5.0.0" && find . -name upgrade.php | \
xargs grep -l 'function.*xmldb_.*_upgrade' | \
grep '/db/' | \
xargs grep -L "Automatically generated Moodle v${rel} release upgrade" | \
xargs perl -p -i -e 's@( *)(return true;)@\1// Automatically generated Moodle v$ENV{rel} release upgrade line.\n\1// Put any upgrade step following this.\n\n\1\2@s'
{code}

*Command to detect* all the upgrade.php files not having those lines:

{code:bash}
find . -name upgrade.php | xargs grep -l 'function.*xmldb_.*_upgrade' | grep '/db/' | xargs grep -L 'Automatically generated Moodle v5.0.0 release upgrade'
{code}

*Commands to detect* that we have not added the lines to incorrect files:

{code:bash}
grep -lr 'Automatically generated Moodle v5.0.0 release upgrade' * | grep -v '/db/'
grep -lr 'Automatically generated Moodle v5.0.0 release upgrade' * | xargs grep -L 'function.*xmldb_.*_upgrade'
{code}

*Command to detect* if the lines have been added after a post-release upgrade step. If there are upgrade steps found, verify that all of them were already there the day of the release and have not been introduced later (you can look for differences between the release v5.0.0 and the current {{main}} branch to verify that)

{code:bash}
export rel="5.0.0" && export ver="202504" &&
find . -name upgrade.php | \
xargs grep -B25 "Automatically generated Moodle v${rel} release upgrade" | \
grep "upgrade_.*_savepoint.*${ver}"
{code}

*Important note to integrators*: The sooner this issue is integrated after release, the fewer chances to get the lines put in an incorrect place (that's what the last "command to detect" above tries to avoid. We need to ensure that the lines are *exactly* at the release point (or we may end up deleting upgrade steps incorrectly in the future). So, immediate integration after release (within the on-sync period and ideally before any new upgrade step is added), it the best achievement.

Ciao :-)

Content loaded with ajax do not get tooltips [after the changes|https://github.com/moodle/moodle/commit/0c586b41c1336202286dcfcb2709cc2f75679c91#diff-b9b5371fe7ffed1862d56df446141c8161732cdae971952b2329a107fa138524L89] in MDL-75669.

The enableTooltips() function in loader.js creates tooltips only for existing elements. To support content updates, it should also listen to filterContentUpdated (core_filters/contentUpdated).

Here's an example implementation to demonstrate (not meant to be copy&pasted)
{code:javascript}const enableTooltips = () => {
    const tooltipTriggerList = document.querySelectorAll('[data-bs-toggle="tooltip"]');
    [...tooltipTriggerList].map(tooltipTriggerEl => new Bootstrap.Tooltip(tooltipTriggerEl));
    document.addEventListener('core_filters/contentUpdated', event => {
        event.detail.nodes.forEach(node => {
            if (node instanceof HTMLElement) {
                const tooltipTriggers = node.querySelectorAll('[data-bs-toggle="tooltip"]');
                [...tooltipTriggers].map(tooltipTrigger => new Bootstrap.Tooltip(tooltipTrigger));
            }
        });
    });
};
{code}

This was fixed in MDL-74814 for {{{}selectgroups{}}}, but this is still a problem for {{{}select{}}}, {{{}tags{}}}, and {{autocomplete}} - possibly others.

The necessary change is to add this to {{export_for_template}} in the {{MoodleQuickForm_select}} class.
{code:java}$context['staticlabel'] = $this->_flagFrozen;{code}

h1. SCORM Player Accessibility Issues: Missing Page Title and Iframe Title Attributes

h2. Summary

The SCORM player in Moodle has two critical accessibility violations:

# Missing page title when SCORM opens in popup mode
# Missing title attribute on the SCORM content iframe

These violations fail WCAG 2.1 Level A requirements and prevent screen reader users from understanding the page context.

h2. Environment

* Moodle version: 4.5 (and earlier versions)
* Affected component: mod/scorm
* Browser: All browsers
* Screen readers affected: JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver, etc.

h2. Issue 1: Missing Page Title in Popup Mode

h3. Description

When a SCORM activity opens in popup mode ({{$displaymode == 'popup'}}), the page title is not set, resulting in an empty {{<title></title>}} element in the HTML head.

h3. Steps to Reproduce

# Create a SCORM activity with "Display in new window" option enabled
# Launch the SCORM activity
# Inspect the popup window's HTML or check the browser tab
# Observe that the {{<title>}} element is empty

h3. Expected Result

The popup window should have a meaningful title, such as the SCORM activity name.

h3. Actual Result

The {{<title>}} element exists but is empty, causing:

* Browser tabs to show "Untitled" or the URL
* Screen readers to announce no page context
* Confusion for users with multiple tabs open

h3. WCAG Violation

* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.4.2 (Page Titled) - Level A*
* Every web page must have a descriptive title that describes topic or purpose

h3. Code Location

File: {{/mod/scorm/player.php}} (lines 113-119)

{noformat}if ($displaymode == 'popup') {
    $PAGE->set_pagelayout('embedded');
} else {
    $shortname = format_string($course->shortname, true, array('context' => $coursecontext));
    $pagetitle = strip_tags("$shortname: ".format_string($scorm->name));
    $PAGE->set_title($pagetitle);
    $PAGE->set_heading($course->fullname);
}
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix

{noformat}if ($displaymode == 'popup') {
    $PAGE->set_pagelayout('embedded');
    // Add page title for popup mode
    $PAGE->set_title(format_string($scorm->name));
} else {
    $shortname = format_string($course->shortname, true, array('context' => $coursecontext));
    $pagetitle = strip_tags("$shortname: ".format_string($scorm->name));
    $PAGE->set_title($pagetitle);
    $PAGE->set_heading($course->fullname);
}
{noformat}

h2. Issue 2: Missing Title Attribute on SCORM Iframe

h3. Description

The iframe that contains the SCORM content ({{id="scorm_object"}}) is created without a title attribute, making it impossible for screen reader users to understand the purpose of the iframe.

h3. Steps to Reproduce

# Open any SCORM activity
# Inspect the page using browser developer tools
# Find the iframe with {{id="scorm_object"}}
# Observe that it has no {{title}} or {{aria-label}} attribute

h3. Expected Result

The iframe should have a descriptive title attribute.

h3. Actual Result

The iframe lacks a title attribute, causing:

* Screen readers to announce "frame" without context
* Users unable to understand what content is in the iframe
* Difficulty navigating between multiple iframes if present

h3. WCAG Violations

* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.4.1 (Bypass Blocks) - Level A*
* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value) - Level A*
* Frames and iframes must have accessible names

h3. Code Location

File: {{/mod/scorm/module.js}} (lines 93-99 in the {{scorm_activate_item}} function)

{noformat}var obj = document.createElement('iframe');
obj.setAttribute('id', 'scorm_object');
obj.setAttribute('type', 'text/html');
obj.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'allowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('webkitallowfullscreen', 'webkitallowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('mozallowfullscreen', 'mozallowfullscreen');
if (!window_name && node.title != null) {
    obj.setAttribute('src', url_prefix + node.title);
}
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix

{noformat}var obj = document.createElement('iframe');
obj.setAttribute('id', 'scorm_object');
obj.setAttribute('type', 'text/html');
obj.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'allowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('webkitallowfullscreen', 'webkitallowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('mozallowfullscreen', 'mozallowfullscreen');
// Add title attribute for accessibility
obj.setAttribute('title', M.util.get_string('scormcontent', 'scorm'));
if (!window_name && node.title != null) {
    obj.setAttribute('src', url_prefix + node.title);
}
{noformat}

h3. Additional Location

The noscript fallback iframe also lacks a title attribute.

File: {{/mod/scorm/player.php}} (lines 228-230)

{noformat}echo html_writer::tag('noscript', html_writer::tag('iframe', '', array('id' => 'main',
    'class' => 'scoframe', 'name' => 'main', 'src' => 'loadSCO.php?id='.$cm->id.$scoidstr.$modestr)));
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix for Noscript

{noformat}echo html_writer::tag('noscript', html_writer::tag('iframe', '', array(
    'id' => 'main',
    'class' => 'scoframe',
    'name' => 'main',
    'src' => 'loadSCO.php?id='.$cm->id.$scoidstr.$modestr,
    'title' => get_string('scormcontent', 'scorm')
)));
{noformat}

h2. Language String Addition

Add a new language string to {{/mod/scorm/lang/en/scorm.php}}:

{noformat}$string['scormcontent'] = 'SCORM content';
{noformat}

h2. Testing Instructions

# Apply the fixes
# Test with screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver)
# Verify page titles appear in browser tabs for popup mode
# Verify screen readers announce iframe purpose
# Run automated accessibility testing tools (axe DevTools, WAVE)

h2. Impact

* *Severity*: High - These are Level A WCAG violations
* *Users affected*: All users relying on screen readers
* *Compliance*: Required for legal accessibility compliance in many jurisdictions

h2. Additional Notes

These issues have been confirmed in Moodle 4.5 but likely exist in earlier versions. Both fixes are minimal code changes that don't affect functionality, only improve accessibility.

This is a follow up to [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85355|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85355|smart-link], because this case was missed there.

Basically, if we don’t have any placement configured for a given tool, and we click “Manage placements” in the course tools tool context menu, we’ll see a funny empty modal. 

There is currently no UX mockup for this case in the prototype, so perhaps a sensible default might be to simply render a warning notification in the form in such cases. E.g.

{noformat}if (empty($statusrecords)) {
    global $OUTPUT;
    // Ignore the hard coded strings here of course...
    $notice = new \core\output\notification('Placements can be configured in the tool\'s configuration.', \core\output\notification::NOTIFY_WARNING, false, 'There are no available placements for this tool', 'i/warning');
    $mform->addElement('html', $OUTPUT->render($notice));
} else {
    // Normal form render stuff..
}{noformat}

And then, once the behat tests have been updated in [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85918|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85918|smart-link], we can also add/extend a scenario in ltix/tests/behat/managecoursetools.feature covering this case (all we’ll need is a tool without a configured placement and we should see it).

On the hub registration form, there are two text boxes that allow you to input a different email to use when receiving email alerts and expert tips:

* {{emailalertemail}}
* {{commnewsemail}}

These emails are sent to the hub and input into their own DB fields.

If an admin changes their mind and decides to toggle off the ‘use different email’, the hub is not made aware of this and will presumably continue to send emails to the stored email values.  This is because we send null values for these params and the hub skips them during its validation, leaving what was originally set.

We need to force a reset of the email values at the hub when this occurs.

Error: 

Default exception handler: Error writing to database Debug: ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint "mdl_userenro_enruse_uix"



The error seems caused by [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-73845|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-73845|smart-link]



For example, suppose a course has three database enrolment instances with IDs *100, 101, and 102*.

User *200* is currently enrolled through enrolment instances *101* and *102*, meaning the user enrolment records are (enrolid, userid):

* (101, 200)
* (102, 200)

There is no enrolment record for (100, 200).

When the script runs, it attempts to reassign the user’s enrolments to the lowest enrol ID (100). This means it tries to update:

* (101, 200) → (100, 200)
* (102, 200) → (100, 200)

However, this creates duplicate records for (100, 200), which violates the *unique constraint* on enrolments.

[https://github.com/moodle/moodle/blob/MOODLE_405_STABLE/enrol/database/db/upgrade.php#L55-L81|https://github.com/moodle/moodle/blob/MOODLE_405_STABLE/enrol/database/db/upgrade.php#L55-L81|smart-link] 



SQL Query to check if a site will be affected by the regression (No record mean 'not affected')

{{SELECT}}
{{       ue.id,}}
{{       e.courseid,}}
{{       ue.userid,}}
{{       ue.enrolid,}}
{{       keeper.id as target_enrol_id}}
{{FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue}}
{{JOIN prefix_enrol e ON ue.enrolid = e.id}}
{{JOIN (}}
{{    SELECT courseid, MIN(id) as id}}
{{    FROM prefix_enrol}}
{{    WHERE enrol = 'database'}}
{{    GROUP BY courseid}}
{{    HAVING COUNT() > 2}}
{{) keeper ON e.courseid = keeper.courseid}}
{{WHERE e.enrol = 'database'}}
{{  AND e.id != keeper.id}}
{{  AND NOT EXISTS (}}
{{      SELECT 1}}
{{      FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue2}}
{{      WHERE ue2.userid = ue.userid}}
{{        AND ue2.enrolid = keeper.id}}
{{  )}}
{{  AND ue.userid IN (}}
{{      SELECT ue3.userid}}
{{      FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue3}}
{{      JOIN prefix_enrol e3 ON ue3.enrolid = e3.id}}
{{      WHERE e3.courseid = e.courseid}}
{{        AND e3.enrol = 'database'}}
{{      GROUP BY ue3.userid}}
{{      HAVING COUNT() >= 2}}
{{  )}}
{{ORDER BY e.courseid, ue.userid, ue.enrolid;}}

